-- title:
--   Order-M points modulo ± H counted by an index
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a natural number with $M \neq 0$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and let $A$ be an additive commutative group together with an isomorphism of additive groups $e : \mathbb{Z}/M \times \mathbb{Z}/M \xrightarrow{\sim} \{a \in A : M \cdot a = 0\}$, the latter being the $M$-torsion submodule of $A$ viewed as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Consider those subsets $s \subseteq A$ for which there is a point $P \in A$ of exact additive order $M$ with $s = \{u' \cdot P : u \in H \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle\}$, where $u$ ranges over the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ generated by $H$ together with $-1$ and $u'$ denotes the canonical natural-number representative of $u$ acting on $A$ by multiplication. The assertion is that the number of such subsets equals the index in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by $\{\pm I\}$ together with [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the set of matrices $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower-right entry reduces mod $M$ to an element of $H$. Both sides are natural numbers, with the usual convention that each is $0$ in the infinite case, so the equality also records the finiteness of the set of such subsets.
--
--   This is the classical count of $\Gamma_H(M)$-level structures taken up to sign: the subsets described are the orbits of the points of exact order $M$ in $A$ under the scalars $\pm H$, and they are in bijection with the cosets of $\pm\Gamma_H(M)$ in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$. It is used in the construction of the function fields of the modular curves of level $\Gamma_H$, for instance by [`ModularCurve.exists_equiv_algHom_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_of_transcendental_j`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_equiv_algHom_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_of_transcendental_j), and rests on the transitivity and stabiliser statement [`CohCarrier.exists_bottomRow_eq_and_torsionOrbit_bottomRow_eq_iff`](thm.html#CohCarrier.exists_bottomRow_eq_and_torsionOrbit_bottomRow_eq_iff) describing bottom rows of integral unimodular matrices modulo $M$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AddCommGroup_natCard_torsionOrbit_gammaH_eq_index.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CohCarrier_Level

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open scoped MatrixGroups

theorem AddCommGroup.natCard_torsionOrbit_gammaH_eq_index
    (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] (H : Subgroup (ZMod M)ˣ) {A : Type*} [AddCommGroup A]
    (e : ZMod M × ZMod M ≃+ Submodule.torsionBy ℤ A M) :
    Nat.card {s : Set A // ∃ P : A, addOrderOf P = M ∧
        s = {T | ∃ u : (ZMod M)ˣ, u ∈ H ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers (-1) ∧ T = (u : ZMod M).val • P}} =
      (CohCarrier.GammaH M H ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers (-1)).index := by sorry
